WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.060
My name is Nick Zammeti

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.550
and I'm a YouTube influencer,

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.340
I suppose, or woodworker, artist.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:15.480
I'm going to walk you

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.410
through how I restore a
rotting Christmas sleigh.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:22.650
I was involved in a TV
series here in the UK,

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.160
which, I got given the sleigh to restore.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.840
It was brought in from Lithuania,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.600
so the sleigh was pretty old.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.640
I'm not too sure exactly how old it was,

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.080
but it could be 100 years old.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.330
I have no idea. But it
was definitely pretty old.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.240
First of all, it's covered in this green,

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:42.300
like a lime-green paint
that somebody's painted,

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.730
and I'm not sure if that was
the original color or not.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.460
It's got twisted bars in it.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.040
The metal's all twisted and battered.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.770
Half the seat's missing on it.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.270
So there's there's certainly
a lot of work to do.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.230
First, what I've got to do
is unbolt all of the sleigh.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:02.250
The best thing to try

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.110
with this type of restoration is to try

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:07.650
and unbolt everything I
can, using different tools

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:10.770
because there has been some
different types of nuts

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.930
and bolts added to this over the period.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:17.310
So I'm trying different spanners
and ratchets and sockets

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.300
and things just to try

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.550
and get everything unbolted that I can.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:32.160
Now I'm going to wire-brush
the entire sleigh as well,

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.950
because I just want to get
off all the rust I can.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:37.080
I'd say it's probably been
on here for years and years.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:41.080
So wire-brushing everything
as much as possible.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:52.200
So, there's bits of the
patterns on the side there,

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.060
some bits that are missing in that.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.093
So I'm going to need to kind of recreate

00:01:56.093 --> 00:01:57.870
and reconstruct those.

00:01:57.870 --> 00:02:01.830
There's an old bit of wood that
I can lose from this to use

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.320
to cut out the pieces.
I'm going to have to chop

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:05.400
out a few of the bits

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.613
and pieces that I need from
that old bit of sleigh wood.

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:12.570
I'm going to use a jigsaw
to cut out the shapes

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.190
for the missing part and then try

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:17.504
and sand it back and glue it in.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.260
What I'm going to have to do to try

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:27.660
and recreate the pattern that's missing

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:31.440
on the other side is just check
out the side that is whole

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.890
and sort of trace that
side and then flip it over

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:37.200
and then try and cut out a similar shape

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.993
to fit into the missing pattern.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.650
Now I'm going to have to make a seat

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:53.640
for this sleigh, because there
isn't one. It's disappeared.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:57.060
So I'm going to biscuit-join
the pieces of wood together

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.823
to try and make the seat a whole piece.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.420
So, when you put the biscuits in,

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.010
I'm going to have to put some glue in

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:09.260
and get it all clamped up
and leave that overnight.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.810
So, now with the seat that's now ready

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:24.120
and all glued up, I'm going to have to try

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:25.590
and rough this up a little bit.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.990
So I'm going to burn it, just
try and make it look a bit old

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:30.420
and sort of, like, in keeping
with the sleigh really,

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:31.860
because it's a new piece of wood.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:34.470
We've had to make this seat
completely from scratch.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:36.150
So really you're going
to have to burn it up,

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.340
bang it with a hammer a few times,

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.257
like it's been there for 100 years.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:53.580
So, now we're going to have
to sand the entire sleigh

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.830
down. As much sanding as possible.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.590
There's going to be a lot
of hand-sanding involved,

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.420
and I'm going to have
to use a few machines

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.950
like orbital sanders

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.430
just to really try and
get as much of this green

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.620
that someone's covered this sleigh in,

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:09.287
and also with the metalwork as well,

00:04:09.287 --> 00:04:11.160
because it is very rusty

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.200
and it's got some really old paint on it.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.750
Going to try and get all
that back to bare metal,

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.450
just to try to get off all the old stuff

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.673
and preparation, really,
for the new paint.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:25.560
I want to paint the frame black.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.190
There's obviously few different
ways to paint sleighs,

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:31.857
but I want a sort of
traditional Santa sleigh,

00:04:31.857 --> 00:04:34.290
and from what I know
and what I've grown up

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.390
to know of is that the
Santa sleigh's kind of,

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:37.950
like, a bit red, obviously,

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.210
and it's got some black in it.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.690
So I'm going to go with
the frame completely black

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.640
and then start painting all the wood

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:47.373
a nice, bright, vibrant Santa-sleigh red.

00:04:51.354 --> 00:04:54.960
The sleigh's going to need
a few coats of this red

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.270
because it's going to seep
into the wood quite a bit.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.220
So we're going to need a
few coats of the red on it.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.900
The black's going to cover quite well,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.040
so that's going to come up all right.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:03.330
And I think with this piece,

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.490
it's going to need hand-painting, really,

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.640
because there are so many
individual little areas

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.940
and little bits that meet
up to the black metal.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:14.163
I think it's just going to be
easier to just hand-paint it.

00:05:14.163 --> 00:05:16.260
It's going to take a lot longer,

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:19.053
but I think the finish is
going to be much, much better.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:24.630
Now I'm going to have to
use a tiny paintbrush, just

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.990
because it's just a bit
more of a detailed section.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:30.450
I want to make sure I
don't get the paint all

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:32.900
over the other paint that
I've just put on there.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.920
So, I've managed to keep all the aluminum

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.960
that's been put around this sleigh.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:44.640
I'm going to have to
put it all back in now.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:47.040
Just basically using some new nails,

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:48.150
just hammer and nails, really,

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:51.120
just making sure it's
all banged into place.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.160
And it is that type of aluminum that

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:56.340
you can just bang it and mold
it around the wood and stuff.

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:59.507
So it makes it look quite cool anyway.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:06.750
Now I'm going to fit everything together.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:09.870
So I'm going to put the
new seat in that I've made,

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:13.912
get that bolted in and secure
with the backrest on there.

00:06:13.912 --> 00:06:15.210
There's a few new bolts

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:16.890
I have to add into this

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:21.223
because some of them couldn't
really get off before.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:33.210
So, that is the sleigh finished.

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:36.360
The end story to this is
actually pretty amazing.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:37.980
Because it was part of the show,

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:40.350
I obviously had to sell this sleigh,

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.150
and it actually was purchased

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:45.450
by a chap who runs a shop in New Zealand.

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:48.870
So if you wanted to see this sleigh

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.840
or actually take a seat in the sleigh,

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.310
it is now sat in New Zealand

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:56.227
in a shop called the Christmas Hut.

